    "narrative": "The lineup for LawDog today is anchored by **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81), **Matt Chapman** (70.06), and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), who all benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Ritchie and his 4.93 xERA. **Geraldo Perdomo** stands out as our premier play; he capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against a weak opposing starter, with the model rewarding his placement in the two-hole. **Matt Chapman** and **Luis Arraez** also see their scores buoyed by the weak pitching environment and optimal order positioning. We are also leaning into **Bryson Stott** (66.79) and **Tyler Freeman** (68.68), both of whom offer strong efficiency scores against mid-tier arms like Alcantara and Assad, respectively, providing a high floor across our middle infield slots.\n\nThe bench decision process was narrow today, specifically regarding **Masyn Winn** (42.87). While **Masyn Winn** remains a valuable asset for our SB-starved build, the combination of a difficult matchup against Rodriguez (3.45 xERA) and the superior efficiency ratings of our starting outfielders kept him on the pine. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Taylor Ward** (45.02), whose score is suppressed by a difficult encounter with Kirby (3.60 xERA). While he carries a risk of underperforming due to the elite opposing arm, his lead-off spot remains the primary driver of his inclusion over deeper bench options. We remain cautious regarding **Jonathan Aranda** (49.62), as facing Ohtani is a negative-EV event that forces us to temper expectations despite his favorable spot in the batting order. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Will Smith** currently sidelined, our depth is being tested; we are relying on the tactical utilization of **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories while navigating these availability constraints.",
